// -*- C++ -*-  THE ACTION TABLE. One file, four artifacts -- decision D1-6.
//
// The enum, the string<->id maps, the default-context map, and the `action.*` catalog key list are
// ALL generated from the rows below. Three things must agree forever -- the enum, `res/ribbon.json`,
// and the translation catalog -- and three hand-maintained lists agree until the first Friday. One
// table makes a typo a build error at the point of the typo.
//
// This file is #included repeatedly with different macro definitions. It has no include guard on
// purpose. Define what you need before including; the defaults below cover the rest.
//
//   RAWPAGE_ACTION(Enumerator, "string.id", DefaultContext, "action.catalog.key")
//   RAWPAGE_ACTION_ALIAS("old.string.id", NewEnumerator)
//
// DefaultContext is a bare KeyContext enumerator -- `Global`, `Viewer`, `Write` -- and the expansion
// site qualifies it.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// FOUR RULES, none of them stylistic:
//
// 1. THE STRING ID IS A PERMANENT PUBLIC NAME. It is written into a user's saved shortcuts and QAT
//    customization, and read back by a later version. Renaming one without an alias row silently
//    destroys that customization (D1-16).
//
// 2. ALIAS ROWS ARE APPENDED AND NEVER DELETED. An alias is how a renamed id keeps resolving. There
//    is no expiry: the user who customized in Stage 7 still has that file in Stage 15.
//
// 3. THE CATALOG KEY IS "action." + THE STRING ID. `tst_actionregistry` asserts it row by row, so a
//    typo in either column fails the build rather than yielding a button with no label. The column is
//    written out rather than derived because `tools/i18n-lint` reads this file as text.
//
// 4. DECLARING IS NOT REGISTERING. ~200 ids are declared here so the ribbon can place them and the
//    catalog can name them; Stage 1 registers only the 60-80 it implements. The rest render as
//    visible, DISABLED buttons -- the honest state -- and `RibbonTabBuilder` distinguishes
//    "arrives in Stage 7" from "not available for this document" in the tooltip.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

#ifndef RAWPAGE_ACTION
#define RAWPAGE_ACTION(Enumerator, StringId, DefaultContext, LabelKey)
#endif

#ifndef RAWPAGE_ACTION_ALIAS
#define RAWPAGE_ACTION_ALIAS(OldStringId, Enumerator)
#endif

