// Added on the user's request 2026-10-03: a press on the rulers' corner box steps `units/rulerUnit`
// to the next unit, wrapping (`core::nextUnit`). An id rather than a click handler for the reason
// the three below give -- a control that is a lambda is one the tool finder and the batch runner
// cannot reach. No chord, so `Features.md` §8 is not touched.
RAWPAGE_ACTION(ViewCycleRulerUnit,     "view.cycleRulerUnit",     Viewer, "action.view.cycleRulerUnit")

// THREE IDS DECLARED AT STAGE 4 T8, on the rule T7's note above states: a feature reachable only
// from a widget is unfinished (D1-7(a)), and `Features.md` §1.3 asks to *"move, lock, and delete
// individual guides; clear all guides"*. Moving one is a DRAG and rightly has no id -- no more
// than a scroll does -- but the other three are menu items, and a menu item is a command or it is
// a lambda the Stage 14 batch runner cannot reach.
//
// **None of them takes an argument, because dispatch does not.** `view.lockGuide` and
// `view.deleteGuide` act on the guide the context menu was raised over, which
// `ui/viewer/GridGuideLayer::setContextGuide` records at that moment -- Stage 1's **I-50** in a
// second place: *what is under the cursor decides, not which call site raised the menu.* Each is
// DISABLED when there is no such guide rather than silently doing nothing.
//
// No `Features.md` §8 row is added: none of the three has a chord, so §10's *"§8 is not touched"*
// still holds for this stage.
RAWPAGE_ACTION(ViewLockGuide,          "view.lockGuide",          Viewer, "action.view.lockGuide")
RAWPAGE_ACTION(ViewDeleteGuide,        "view.deleteGuide",        Viewer, "action.view.deleteGuide")
RAWPAGE_ACTION(ViewClearGuides,        "view.clearGuides",        Viewer, "action.view.clearGuides")

