// TWO IDS DECLARED AT STAGE 4 T7, and the reason is worth reading before adding a third.
//
// `Stage4-ViewingSurface-Plan.md` §2's inherited ledger says this stage *"declares no new id"* --
// but that line is a MEASUREMENT of the 70 ids already in this stage's namespaces, taken before
// anyone checked whether every Stage 4 feature had one. Two do not: `Features.md` §1.2 lists the
// Loupe and auto-scroll, `Stage4-ViewingSurface-Plan.md` §6 gives both to T7, and neither had a
// row here nor a chord in §8.
//
// The standing rule decides it: *no feature that the headless batch path (flow K) cannot reach --
// reachable only from a widget means unfinished*. Building a tool nobody can dispatch would have
// broken that; deferring two features the plan schedules would have been a scope cut. So both get
// a name, and **neither gets a §8 binding** -- `Features.md` §8 is untouched by this stage (plan
// §10), and `pane.destinations` at T6 is the precedent for a registered id with no default chord.
//
// THERE IS NO THIRD ID FOR *REVERSE*. Speed and direction are one signed value,
// `pageDisplay/autoScrollSpeed`, so reverse is a negative number reachable from Preferences, the
// settings file and the batch runner. Minting a permanent public name for the sign of a number
// that already has a home is the thing this comment exists to prevent.
RAWPAGE_ACTION(ToolLoupe,              "tool.loupe",              Viewer, "action.tool.loupe")

// --- Full Screen and Presentation (§1.2, §8's Full Screen table) --------------------------------
